# State management

- Keep state as close as possible to where it is used
- Lift state only when siblings must share it
- Use context sparingly; prefer composition
- Separate UI state from server/cache state
- Prefer React Query / TanStack Query for server state when fetching
- Use simple `useState` first; `useReducer` or a state machine for complex UI flows
- Pair mutations with loading and error states; use optimistic updates when UX benefits
